msgid "Integer"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:115
msgid "How bright (:code:`R+G+B`) does a pixel need to be in order to be recognized as a light source? Increasing this threshold requires brighter light sources (i.e. more white or less color, respectively) but prevents some «false alarms» where semi-bright parts, e.g. hands where colors can change quite a lot compared to the background, are incorrectly recognized as light source."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:116
msgid "Difference threshold"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:118
msgid "How much does the strongest color channel of a pixel have to change, compared to the background image (:code:`max(dR, dG, dB)`), in order to be recognized as light source? Increasing this threshold makes it harder for light sources to be accepted on bright backgrounds, but decreases the danger of noise or generally bright spots counting as light source."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:119
msgid "Difference sum threshold"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:121
msgid "How much does the sum of all color channels *relative to the background image* (:code:`dR + dG + dB`) have to change until a pixel is recognized as a light source? Raising this value might, in some cases, avoid that some light objects lit by the light source are added to the light mask."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:122
msgid "Sensitivity"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:124
msgid "For slowly moving light source try to use a lower sensitivity to obtain a better exposure."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:125
msgid "Lower overexposure"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:127
msgid "The light mask does not get white immediately when the light source is moving slowly or staying steady."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:128
msgid "Dimming"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:130
msgid "Dims the light mask. Lights will leave a fainting trail if it is set to a value > 0."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:131
msgid "Background weight"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:133
msgid "Strength of the (calculated) background image. Setting it to 100 paints the light mask directly over the background, without the painting person in the image if the video starts with a «clean» background image. (See the α parameter.)"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:134
msgid "α"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:136
msgid "Determines how the effect tries to adapt to background changes. The Light Graffiti effect remembers the first frame of the clip it is applied to, so the clip should *always* start with the painter outside of the video. If the background constantly changes, e.g. on a street, try to set α > 0 to calculate an average background image."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:137
msgid "Saturation"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: ../../effects_and_filters/video_effects/stylize/lightgraffiti.rst:139
msgid "Increases the saturation of lights."
msgstr ""

